      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Topological insulators and the quantum spin Hall effect revealed robust electronic phases with organizing principles beyond conventional symmetry breaking.",
        "attribution": "Kane and Mele developed pivotal theoretical predictions, and Molenkamp's experiments established the quantum spin Hall phase in a material system.",
        "maturity": "The effects have been confirmed across materials and have reshaped condensed-matter research.",
        "uncertainties": ["The proposed credit emphasizes the early quantum spin Hall work; later three-dimensional topological insulators involved additional major contributors."]
